# The icon slots, in one pass: what replaced the "> ", "* ", "#" and "+" the rows used to carry.
#
# Messages first, because the leading slot is doing the most work there - a tag for a channel,
# a globe for the view over all of them, a plus on the row that starts a thread, and the reply
# arrow on a preview whose last word was ours. Then the two lists whose marker column says
# something a character could not: which node is us, which the radio has forgotten, which
# device is Bluetooth and which is the one we are attached to - and, since a plain row has a
# marker gutter of its own, which two nodes are pinned. Then the settings root and the Modules
# list under it, which are the leading slot's own callers: one icon per section, in the place
# the eye reaches before it has read a word. Then a settings section, where the pencil says
# Left and Right act on a row and the dot says it has been changed and not yet saved.
#
# The tab strip's own fallback - at a glyph scale where five labels do not fit it labels only
# the tab you are on - needs a scale set before the first frame, so it is its own capture:
#
#     ./scripts/ui-capture.sh -s 6 -o tabs-large.gif <<< 'scene demo'
scene demo
scale 4
delay 260

# The radio's settings, so the Settings rows below are real values rather than "not loaded".
config

# Two pinned nodes, which is a fact no press this harness can make will set.
pin ECHO
pin GOLF

hold 600
tab nodes
hold 700
tab devices
hold 700

# The section list, one icon per row.
tab settings
hold 900

# Settings > Display: three editable rows, then one of them changed.
key down 4
key a
hold 600
key down 3
key right
hold 900

# The first B discards the pending edit, the second leaves the section, which parks the cursor
# back on Display. Then Modules, the other list of subjects.
key b
key b
hold 500
key down 7
key a
hold 900
key b
hold 500

# Messages last, because the leading slot says the most there.
tab messages
hold 900
